-- Old-system expense history -> the fees section (user, Aug 28: 'make sure
-- all are imported by migration'). 4,240 entries from report-expense-income
-- (Jul 2024 - Aug 2026), fee_type 'expense', label = the de-duplicated Khmer
-- category, created_by_name 'Old system' as the dataset marker.
--
-- Expected after applying: 4,240 marker rows, SUM(amount_usd) = 129,696.60,
-- SUM(amount_khr) = 82,419,900 - equal to the source report's own grand
-- total (verified against the file before this migration was generated).
--
-- The DELETE makes this idempotent-by-construction: D1 migration tracking
-- already runs it once, but if the standalone SQL in the migration pack was
-- ever run manually first, this clears exactly that dataset (the marker
-- identifies it and nothing else) before inserting, so rows can never double.
DELETE FROM fees WHERE created_by_name = 'Old system';
